## Colors &amp; Vectors ## {#colors-and-vectors}

<script type=idl>
dictionary GPUColorDict {
    required double r;
    required double g;
    required double b;
    required double a;
};
typedef (sequence<double> or GPUColorDict) GPUColor;
</script>

Note: `double` is large enough to precisely hold 32-bit signed and unsigned integers, as well as single-precision floating point numbers.

<script type=idl>
dictionary GPUOrigin2DDict {
    GPUIntegerCoordinate x = 0;
    GPUIntegerCoordinate y = 0;
};
typedef (sequence<GPUIntegerCoordinate> or GPUOrigin2DDict) GPUOrigin2D;
</script>

<dfn dfn>Origin2D</dfn> is a {{GPUOrigin2D}}.
[=Origin2D=] is a namespace defined below for convenience:
<!-- This is silly, but provides convenient syntax for the spec. -->

<div algorithm="GPUOrigin2D accessors" dfn-for=Origin2D>
    For a given {{GPUOrigin2D}} value |origin|, depending on its type, the syntax:

      - |origin|.<dfn dfn>x</dfn> refers to either {{GPUOrigin2DDict}}.{{GPUOrigin2DDict/x}} or the first item of the sequence, and defaults to 0 if not present.
      - |origin|.<dfn dfn>y</dfn> refers to either {{GPUOrigin2DDict}}.{{GPUOrigin2DDict/y}} or the second item of the sequence, and defaults to 0 if not present.
</div>

<script type=idl>
dictionary GPUOrigin3DDict {
    GPUIntegerCoordinate x = 0;
    GPUIntegerCoordinate y = 0;
    GPUIntegerCoordinate z = 0;
};
typedef (sequence<GPUIntegerCoordinate> or GPUOrigin3DDict) GPUOrigin3D;
</script>

<dfn dfn>Origin3D</dfn> is a {{GPUOrigin3D}}.
[=Origin3D=] is a namespace defined below for convenience:
<!-- This is silly, but provides convenient syntax for the spec. -->

<div algorithm="GPUOrigin3D accessors" dfn-for=Origin3D>
    For a given {{GPUOrigin3D}} value |origin|, depending on its type, the syntax:

      - |origin|.<dfn dfn>x</dfn> refers to either {{GPUOrigin3DDict}}.{{GPUOrigin3DDict/x}} or the first item of the sequence, and defaults to 0 if not present.
      - |origin|.<dfn dfn>y</dfn> refers to either {{GPUOrigin3DDict}}.{{GPUOrigin3DDict/y}} or the second item of the sequence, and defaults to 0 if not present.
      - |origin|.<dfn dfn>z</dfn> refers to either {{GPUOrigin3DDict}}.{{GPUOrigin3DDict/z}} or the third item of the sequence, and defaults to 0 if not present.
</div>

<script type=idl>
dictionary GPUExtent3DDict {
    required GPUIntegerCoordinate width;
    GPUIntegerCoordinate height = 1;
    GPUIntegerCoordinate depthOrArrayLayers = 1;
};
typedef (sequence<GPUIntegerCoordinate> or GPUExtent3DDict) GPUExtent3D;
</script>

<dfn dfn>Extent3D</dfn> is a {{GPUExtent3D}}.
[=Extent3D=] is a namespace defined below for convenience:
<!-- This is silly, but provides convenient syntax for the spec. -->

<div algorithm="GPUExtent3D accessors" dfn-for=Extent3D>
    For a given {{GPUExtent3D}} value |extent|, depending on its type, the syntax:

      - |extent|.<dfn dfn>width</dfn> refers to either {{GPUExtent3DDict}}.{{GPUExtent3DDict/width}} or the first item of the sequence, and defaults to 1 if not present.
      - |extent|.<dfn dfn>height</dfn> refers to either {{GPUExtent3DDict}}.{{GPUExtent3DDict/height}} or the second item of the sequence, and defaults to 1 if not present.
      - |extent|.<dfn dfn>depthOrArrayLayers</dfn> refers to either {{GPUExtent3DDict}}.{{GPUExtent3DDict/depthOrArrayLayers}} or the third item of the sequence, and defaults to 1 if not present.
</div>

