#### Reading and sampling depth/stencil textures #### {#reading-depth-stencil}

When a depth component is read or sampled via a `texture_depth_*`-type binding, the value is returned as an `f32` value.

Issue(gpuweb/gpuweb#2094): Depending on the resolution of this issue, allow reading/sampling via `texture_2d` etc. from the table above, and specify the behavior. (`vec4<f32>(D, X, X, X)`?) Update the note below, which will be slightly out of date. [issue#gpuweb/gpuweb#2094]

A stencil component must be read or sampled via a normal texture binding (`texture_2d`, `texture_2d_array`, `texture_cube`, or `texture_cube_array`). When doing so, the value is returned as `vec4<u32>(S, X, X, X)`, where S is the stencil value and each X is an implementation-defined unspecified value.

Authors cannot rely on the .y, .z, and .w components, as their behavior is not portable.

Note: Without adding a new, more-constrained stencil sampler type (like depth), it is not feasible for implementations to effectively mask over driver differences in stencil reads. As this was not a portability pain point for WebGL, it is expected to not be an issue in WebGPU. In practice, depending on the hardware, either `vec4<u32>(S, S, S, S)` or `vec4<u32>(S, 0, 0, 1)` is required.

#### Copying depth/stencil textures #### {#copying-depth-stencil}

The texel values of the depth32float formats ({{GPUTextureFormat/"depth32float"}} and {{GPUTextureFormat/"depth32float-stencil8"}}) have a limited range. Copying into such textures is therefore only valid from other textures of the same format.
<!-- Update this if an unrestricted-depth feature is added. -->

The depth aspect of the depth24plus formats ({{GPUTextureFormat/"depth24plus"}} and {{GPUTextureFormat/"depth24plus-stencil8"}}) has an opaque representation (implemented as either "depth24unorm" or "depth32float"). The depth aspect of {{GPUTextureFormat/"depth24unorm-stencil8"}} does not have an aligned, tightly packed representation (because its size is 3 bytes). Image copies ([=image copies=]) of the depth aspect are therefore not allowed for these formats.

<div class=note>
    It is possible to imitate these disallowed copies:

    - All of these formats can be written in a render pass using a fragment shader that outputs
        depth values via the `frag_depth` output.
    - Textures with "depth24plus"/"depth24unorm" formats can be read as shader textures, and
        written to a texture (as a render pass attachment) or
        buffer (via a storage buffer binding in a compute shader).
</div>

### Packed formats ### {#packed-formats}

All packed texture formats support the {{GPUTextureUsage/COPY_SRC}}, {{GPUTextureUsage/COPY_DST}}, and {{GPUTextureUsage/TEXTURE_BINDING}} usages. All of those that have the {{GPUTextureSampleType/"float"}} type can be filtered when sampled. None of these formats support multisampling.

A <dfn dfn>compressed format</dfn> is any format with a block size greater than 1 &times; 1.

